title: Agitation in the Occupied Ruhr
subtitle: French troops in the mines, nationalists in the streets, prices doubling every week.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: rf_mass
view-if: rf_ruhr_timer <= 0 and year = 1923 and month <= 10
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rf_ruhr_timer = 3

= Agitation in the Occupied Ruhr

The party's slogan is "Beat Poincaré on the Ruhr and Cuno on the Spree": fight the French occupation and the German government that profits from it at the same time. How to say it is another question.

- @both
- @french
- @national

@both
title: Against Poincaré and Cuno alike.
subtitle: Brings in members. Pleases the <span class="f-left">Left</span>.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {left: 3});
Q.members += 10;
Q.rev_situation += 3;
Q.repression += 3;
!}

Communist speakers denounce both governments at pit-head meetings. Membership in the Ruhr grows.

@french
title: Work with the French Communists among the occupying soldiers.
subtitle: Pleases Moscow and <span class="f-stalin">Thälmann</span>.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.obey(Q, 4);
Q.members += 3;
Q.repression += 2;
!}

Activists of the <span class="p-kpd">KPD</span> and the <span class="p-pcf">French Communist Party</span> hand out leaflets urging French soldiers not to fire on German workers. It is internationalism in practice, and the <span class="p-comintern">Comintern</span> approves. German nationalists call it treason.

@national
title: Speak the nationalists' language to win their followers.
subtitle: Brings in members. Pleases the <span class="f-right">Right</span>. Angers the <span class="f-left">Left</span>, the <span class="f-ultra">Ultra-Left</span> and the <span class="p-spd">SPD</span>.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 2, left: -3, ultra: -3});
Q.members += 8;
Q.spd_relation -= 4;
!}

Party speakers attack the occupation in national terms and court young nationalists. Some are won over. Many old members are uneasy, and the <span class="p-spd">SPD</span> says the Communists now sound like the Freikorps.
